00:51:12.710 --> 00:51:14.900
Probably the good people, actually, they
go.

00:51:14.900 --> 00:51:18.570
I'm not that good, so I stay, but, and
they go on and they build.

00:51:18.570 --> 00:51:22.390
So I'm very keen, what, what is it that
we're going to do to ensure

00:51:22.390 --> 00:51:26.870
we're producing more CEOs and other
leaders if you will as we go through it.

00:51:26.870 --> 00:51:28.620
What we've done is we revamped our people

00:51:28.620 --> 00:51:30.500
process we done a number of different
things.

00:51:30.500 --> 00:51:32.800
When I mentioned this tri-sector athlete
piece,

00:51:32.800 --> 00:51:34.590
what we're doing is we've, that's why

00:51:34.590 --> 00:51:36.870
it's vital for us in having a

00:51:36.870 --> 00:51:40.220
social sector practice and a public sector
practice.

00:51:40.220 --> 00:51:42.210
There, there's important work to be done
there but

00:51:42.210 --> 00:51:44.360
frankly the reason, the big reason why we
have

00:51:44.360 --> 00:51:46.250
that is cuz we want people to have
experience

00:51:46.250 --> 00:51:48.920
and working with those institutions, with
